message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Compiled World Runtime"
abstract: >-
  The Compiled World Runtime (CWR) is a runtime in which an AI model acts by running scripts
  inside a compiled, rule-governed world. A human-edited World Source is compiled into an
  immutable, content-addressed Build. The World Kernel runs each script in a sandbox through
  atomic primitives whose outcomes depend only on visible conditions, records every action in a
  hash-chained ledger and mediates every call to an outside service. The rules change only when a
  human recompiles the world into a new, versioned Build that the model is told about.
authors:
